**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests`

**How to implement.** The category store over the library database, with the built-in-not-removable rule read from the provenance (001 §C 'What it holds': categories; 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite `create`'; .spec-md §0.2 Storage row). (1) `MaterialLibrary.fs`: `CategoryError` gains `CategoryStoreUnavailableErr of reason : string`, the category store beneath the proxy failed, carrying the failure's `describe`. Every complete match on `CategoryError` gains it: `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:CategoryError.caption` and `CatalogueImport.fs`'s category reason (step 37). The `CategoryProxy` doc names `CategoryProxy.createInDatabase` beside the in-memory store. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CategoryDatabaseStore.fs`, `module CategoryDatabaseStore`, compiled directly after `MaterialDatabaseStore.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type CategoryProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : CategoryProxy` carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, "the SQLite category store (001 §C): every field is one LibraryDatabase.run over the entry-version rows")>]`. As in step 69, every field is one `run` over step 67's operations with one `SaveChanges ()` per write, and every `StorageError` or decoder `LibraryEntryError` is `CategoryStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`. An entry is a category when its latest row's kind is `CategoryEntryKind`. The fields: `listCategories ()` decodes (`toMaterialCategory`) the latest version of every category, whatever its lifecycle, sorted by id as the in-memory map lists them; `addCategory c` runs `c.validate` first, answers `duplicateCategory` of the category already holding the id, `DuplicateCategoryIdErr` naming the id and the `extension` of another kind holding it, and otherwise stages `stageNewEntry` of `LibraryEntryContent.ofMaterialCategory VersionNumber.first provenance c`, where a `BuiltInCategory` is filed under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` (step 32, the one built-in catalogue) and a `UserCategory` under `UserProvenance`, because the origin derives from the provenance (step 24); `updateCategory c` runs `c.validate`, answers `unknownCategory` without a category, builds `ofMaterialCategory` at the latest's version under the latest's provenance, which an update keeps, so a category whose origin disagrees with that provenance is `InvalidCategoryErr` carrying the builder's `describe`, and stages `stageEdit` of the latest with the `decideVersioning` of the stored and the incoming category's `{ physics = visibility; metadata = name }` over the latest's pin; nothing pins a category in this section, so an update acts in place as the in-memory store's does; `removeCategory id` answers `unknownCategory` without a category, `builtInNotRemovable` when its decoded origin is `BuiltInCategory` (a built-in catalogue's entry is protected), and `stillReferenced` naming each material whose latest version, active or not, has the category, as `materialsReferencingCategory` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:materialsReferencingCategory`) reads `IncludeInactive`, read inside the same `run`; else it stages `stageRemoval`. Every refusal but the cross-kind `DuplicateCategoryIdErr` is step 70's member. No cache, retry or category pin verb is added. (3) Tests, in `CategoryProxyTests.fs`: `type CategoryProxySqliteTests () = inherit CategoryProxyContract ()` runs the contract's facts (step 66) over one `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` per fact, `stores` answering `CategoryProxy.createInDatabase` and `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase` (step 69) of it, and implements `IDisposable` to dispose it. Its own facts: `a category's provenance follows its origin, and an update keeps it`: read through `run` and `tryLatestStored`, a `UserCategory` added is version 1 under `UserProvenance`; a `BuiltInCategory` added is version 1 under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` and refuses `removeCategory` with `BuiltInNotRemovableErr`; Glass renamed keeps version 1 and its built-in provenance; and Glass updated with `origin = UserCategory` answers `InvalidCategoryErr` and leaves the row as it was. `a database failure below the category store is CategoryStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`: over a disposed database every field answers `Error (CategoryStoreUnavailableErr _)`.

**Acceptance.** After the database store lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every CategoryProxyContract fact under `CategoryProxySqliteTests` and its own `a category's provenance follows its origin, and an update keeps it` and `a database failure below the category store is CategoryStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 10; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.
